    "chunk_text": "Today the government has failed to provide security to even the prisoners. There are many shootings happening in different parts of the country. The government should take steps to ensure that there is more national security. I ensure that under a future regime of ours we would ensure the security of the people.\n\nWe did not oppose the government\u2019s act of arresting our former Organizer. The government can\u2019t take action against people who have committed an offence. But he is not yet proven guilty regarding the issue. As a Party we have cancelled his party membership.\n\nThe investigations allegedly revealed that a business person, attached to the JVP, has funded the Easter bombings. Why is the government hiding these facts? Two sons of a JVP candidate were involved in this group who committed suicide. We urge the government to act on these parties too\n\nA court case has been filed against the Minister of Energy over a corruption that occurred when he was in the Fertilizer Corporation. What are the actions taken by the Government? A Deputy Cabinet Minister and a Mayor were convicted over a matter related to a building. I would like to question the government on what did they do about it as well.\n\nQ While your party complained against the 22nd Amendment to the Constitution, those supporting the government argue that the culture of interfering with the judiciary and the chief justice started from the time of J. R. Jayewardene, the leader of your mother party UNP and the procedure was followed by Chandrika\u2019s government and then byMahinda Rajapaksa. What is your say?"
