    "md5": "f5a0a05be0b1e55b4419bb4aded66f82",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1724,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka rings bell for responsible business\n\nCeremonial CSE bell-ringing marks UN Global Compact launch of Responsible Business Coalition\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) and the UN Global Compact yesterday marked a milestone in advancing responsible business in Sri Lanka with a ceremonial \u2018Ring the Bell for Responsible Business\u2019 event and the launch of the Responsible Business Coalition\u2014a landmark partnership designed to embed sustainability, strengthened governance and the Ten Principles of the UN Global Compact across the country\u2019s business leadership.\n\nThe engagement formed a flagship moment during the visit of UN Global Compact CEO/Executive Director Sanda Ojiambo, bringing together business leaders, listed companies, think tanks, and professional and industry associations in a shared commitment to accelerate responsible business leadership in Sri Lanka.\n\nHeld at the Colombo Stock Exchange, the ceremony saw Sanda Ojiambo join senior leadership from the Colombo Stock Exchange in ringing the opening bell, symbolising the vital role of capital markets in advancing responsible business and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Timed to coincide with the opening of the trading day, the ceremony reflected the growing recognition that long-term business success is intrinsically linked to sustainability, transparency and responsible corporate governance.\n\nIn her address to the trading floor, Ojiambo highlighted the increasingly important role of the private sector in building resilient, inclusive and sustainable economies, noting that responsible business is no longer simply a matter of corporate responsibility, but a strategic imperative for long-term competitiveness and resilience."
  },
