    "chunk_size_bytes": 816,
    "chunk_text": "Over 1,000 foreigners arrested in cybercrime raids this year\n\nColombo, Aug 13 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka Police have arrested 1,093 foreign nationals suspected of involvement in cybercrime and financial fraud during 24 raids conducted so far this year.\n\nPolic Spokesperson ASP F.U. Wootler disclosed the figures at a press conference today (13) held to raise awareness about the \u2018Ratama Ekata\u2019 national operation.\n\nAccording to Wootler, police arrested 573 foreign nationals in 26 incidents in 2024, while 26 foreign nationals were arrested in two incidents in 2025.\n\nThe number of arrests has risen sharply this year, with 1,093 foreign suspects taken into custody during 24 raids.\n\nASP Wootler said legal procedures are currently underway to deport the arrested foreign nationals to their respective countries."
  },
