    "md5": "e2c823b3fbcf4ad9a549b6790b5d62ea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1277,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka to host World CIO 200 Awards and Roadshow 2026 in September\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has approved Sri Lanka to host the 2026 edition of the \u201cWorld CIO 200 Awards and Roadshow\u201d and an international \u201cTech Marathon\u201d in September.\n\nThe four-day World CIO 200 program is expected to bring together over 400 senior executives from over 50 countries, including chief information officers, digital transformation leaders, innovators, investors and business executives.\n\nThe program will feature an international conference, leadership forums, business networking sessions, investment promotion activities, business-to-business meetings, an exhibition and an awards ceremony.\n\nThe international \u201cTech Marathon\u201d will be held alongside the program, with a focus on promoting innovation, youth participation, sports tourism and community engagement.\n\nThe World CIO 200 Awards and Roadshow is organised globally by GEC Media Group, while HTP Global Technologies LLC will manage and finance the Sri Lankan program at its own expense.\n\nThe proposal to this effect was submitted by Science and Technology Minister Prof. Chrishantha Abeysena to host both programmes in Sri Lanka, citing their potential economic, tourism, investment and strategic benefits to the country."
  },
