    "chunk_size_bytes": 967,
    "chunk_text": "Wattala shooting suspects deported from India\n\nColombo, August 14 (Daily Mirror) - Two suspects allegedly involved in a fatal shooting at a birthday party held at a hotel in Wattala on the night of July 23 have been arrested at Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) in Katunayake after fleeing to India.\n\nAccording to police, the suspects allegedly escaped to India by boat following the shooting. While hiding there, they were arrested by Indian security forces and subsequently deported to Sri Lanka.\n\nIndian authorities had informed Criminal Investigation Department (CID) officers at the BIA in advance of the suspects\u2019 deportation from Chennai.\n\nThe two suspects, aged 30 and 34, are residents of the Wattala area.\n\nFollowing the recording of their initial statements by BIA CID officers, the suspects were handed over to the Western Province North Crimes Division for further investigations.\n\nTwo Sri Lankans suspected in Wattala shooting detained in India"
