    "chunk_text": "ROI is measured through strategic growth driven by our insights. When a corporate campaign goes live, we gauge where the audience stood beforehand, analyze their real-time reactions, and formulate a communication strategy based on those emotions. Seeing tangible positive growth in brand equity and public sentiment from that tailored communication is the direct return on investment.\n\nQ Everyone is talking about AI. How does it fit into communications?\n\nAI is incredibly valuable for processing large amounts of information quickly, but it does not replace experience or judgment. PR is built on relationships, trust, and understanding context. Technology highlights what is happening, but people determine what it means and how best to respond. AI is an enabler that strengthens our work, but the human element remains irreplaceable.\n\nQ Are Sri Lankan businesses ready for this, and which industries benefit the most?\n\nI believe they are increasingly aware of its value. Today, customer opinions across digital platforms influence purchasing decisions, investor confidence, and brand trust. Building that trust requires understanding stakeholder sentiments and responding meaningfully. Many leading local and global organizations have already integrated social intelligence into their decision-making processes for a competitive advantage. Any organization with a public reputation benefits, and we see strong interest across banking, insurance, retail, hospitality, tourism, FMCG, and manufacturing.\n\nQ There are many PR agencies today. What differentiates Mark&Comm?\n\nOur strength lies in combining strategic communications with data-driven intelligence. We do not just tell clients what is being said about them; we help them understand why it matters, the potential impact, and how they should respond.\n\nQ Where do you see communications heading over the next five years?"
  },
