    "chunk_text": "The initiative comes as Sri Lanka seeks to build the computing, data and skills infrastructure necessary to expand the use of AI across the government and wider economy, while reducing dependence on the overseas capabilities. The two sides also discussed accelerating Sri Lanka\u2019s digital television project, with Weeraratne calling for outstanding practical issues to be resolved to speed up implementation. The government also raised the possibility of manufacturing digital television set-top boxes locally, instead of relying entirely on imports. Set-top boxes are required for households with compatible analogue television sets to receive digital television signals.\n\nJapan has been a key development partner in Sri Lanka\u2019s shift towards digital terrestrial television, with the country adopting Japan\u2019s Integrated Services Digital Broadcasting-Terrestrial or ISDB-T, standard.\n\nThe latest discussions signal an effort to broaden that technology partnership beyond broadcasting into AI infrastructure and digital public services as Sri Lanka steps up implementation of its digital economy agenda.\n\nThe meeting was also attended by Digital Economy Ministry Secretary Waruna Sri Dhanapala, Senior Presidential Adviser on Digital Economy and GovTech Chairman Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya and JICA Sri Lanka Chief Representative Shigeki Honsu.\n\nThe Digital Economy Ministry said it appreciated the JICA\u2019s technical cooperation and that the government would work to advance the proposed initiatives while strengthening Sri Lanka-Japan cooperation."
